    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Benztropine for extrapyramidal disorders due to neuroleptics: 1 to 4 mg once or twice a day orally, individualized; when they develop soon after starting the neuroleptic (likely transient), one to 2 mg two or three times a day usually gives relief within one or two days; after one or two weeks withdraw it to see if it's still needed."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Not recommended in tardive dyskinesia:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " antiparkinsonism agents don't relieve it and in some instances may aggravate it."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Benztropine may cause anhidrosis:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " use caution in hot weather, especially with other atropine-like drugs or manual labor in heat. With phenothiazines, haloperidol or other anticholinergic or antidopaminergic drugs, report GI complaints, fever or heat intolerance promptly (paralytic ileus, hyperthermia and heat stroke have sometimes been fatal)."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Anticholinergic intoxication:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " physostigmine 1 to 2 mg SC or IV reportedly reverses symptoms; otherwise treatment is symptomatic and supportive."
     }
    ]
   }
  ]
 },
